<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lake Ngami</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lake Ngami is a shallow, often seasonal lake in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/botswana">Botswana</a>, fed by overflow from the Okavango delta. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david-livingstone">David Livingstone</a>'s party reached it in 1849, bringing it to European attention. In the 19th century the Batawana settled nearby, and the area became the centre of their chiefdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lake-ngami.jpg" alt="Lake Ngami" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: From a drawing made on the spot 1850, by the late Alfred Ryder, Esq. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lake_Ngami-1857.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
